cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyCodeCommenter in your research or project, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: PyCodeCommenter
abstract: >
  PyCodeCommenter writes, validates and measures Python docstrings. It reads
  a function's signature and body with Python's ast module to state what the
  code proves (parameters, types, defaults, raise conditions, boolean return
  checks), keeps text the author already wrote, and marks what only a person
  can say. It validates existing docstrings against the code and measures
  documentation coverage. It is deterministic by default; optional AI
  drafting fills the remaining gaps and labels every drafted line for review.
